 typedef void (*dpc_func) (void *arg);
 
+/* Lifetime contract: an external handle/image lease must cover every API call,
+ * including callers paused before acquiring the internal lock. Successful delete
+ * requires exclusive lifecycle custody and no remaining producer leases. Internal
+ * locking does not make raw handles safe after free. Only one delete attempt is
+ * permitted; an error retains queue, callback and module/dependency backing and
+ * forbids replay against recycled thread/semaphore IDs. Self-delete is rejected
+ * without mutation. Callbacks execute unlocked and may requeue while open.
+ * queue_dpc B_OK transfers callback ownership at publication, even if wakeup
+ * subsequently fails. All rejection statuses precede publication. Sticky wakeup
+ * uncertainty prevents successful deletion. new_dpc_queue can return an error
+ * with a non-NULL handle after ambiguous worker start: retain that handle and all
+ * image dependencies; do not retry start or deletion. Layout remains v1.
+ */
 typedef struct {
 	module_info	info;
 
